# SHA-256 of every upstream file this SDK ships unmodified from the official
# mimalloc v3.5.3 release tarball.
#
#   https://github.com/microsoft/mimalloc/releases/download/v3.5.3/mimalloc-v3.5.3-source.tar.gz
#   released 2026-09-17, 1458292 bytes
#   sha256 43857a9e4f26412e970cbe49635d0465c2de6e77a697ce3d4b926a473d1045ca
#
# 52 records, 1166419 bytes: LICENSE, README.upstream.md (the tarball's own
# `readme.md`), SECURITY.md, all 12 headers under `include/` and all 37 files
# under `src/` (31 `.c`, 2 `.h`, two `readme.md`, `etw.man` and
# `etw-mimalloc.wprp`).
#
# This is the complete *compiled and installed closure*, not the complete
# tarball. Upstream's release also ships `docs/`, `test/`, `cmake/`, `ide/`,
# `bin/`, `contrib/` and the top-level `CMakeLists.txt`, none of which this
# package vendors; UPSTREAM.md, "What was not taken", says why, per directory.
# Nothing listed below was dropped for size, and nothing was edited: these are
# the tarball's bytes.
#
# `src/static.c` appears here and is *not* compiled by this build. It travels
# because dropping an upstream file is a claim that needs its own record, and
# UPSTREAM.md records it instead.
#
# `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256` from the repository root checks the bytes.
# A plain checksum run cannot see a file that was added under `include/` or
# `src/` without a record, so the file *set* is a separate claim from the
# digests; see UPSTREAM.md, "What was taken".
#
